  "id": "Compound::DB04920 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Clevidipine is shown to bind to Cyp2e1 and Cyp2d6, both of which are involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to their participation in the epoxygenase and monooxygenase activities, which are ultimately linked to the participation of Cyp2c9. The shared pathway through arachidonic acid metabolism suggests a potential mechanism by which Clevidipine may influence Cyp2c9's function. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a plausible, biologically relevant interaction. The core mechanism involves clevidipine's ability to modulate the activity of cytochrome P450 enzymes, potentially affecting the metabolism of arachidonic acid and its downstream products. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Clevidipine may exert a pharmacological effect on Cyp2c9 through this metabolic pathway.",
